From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yocto Port <elmermetrasbrum@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: radxa-zero-3e: enable UART4

UART4 defaults to status = "disabled" in the shared rk356x.dtsi, on
the uart4m0_xfer pinmux group - which isn't wired to any pin on this
board's 40-pin GPIO header at all. Radxa's own hardware-interface docs
(https://docs.radxa.com/en/zero/zero3/hardware-design/hardware-interface)
and an independent FreeBSD forum thread specifically about this exact
board
(https://forums.freebsd.org/threads/enabling-uarts-on-rk3566-radxa-zero-3e.101491/)
agree: the pins actually routed out are pin 16 (UART4_RX, GPIO3_B1)
and pin 18 (UART4_TX, GPIO3_B2) - the uart4m1_xfer group
(rk3568-pinctrl.dtsi), confirmed against that exact GPIO bank/pin
pair, not just a label name match.

Verified this patch applies cleanly against a pristine checkout of
this exact source (radxa/kernel, linux-6.1-stan-rkr5.1) before adding
it here.

Appears on the target as /dev/ttyS4.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Yocto Port <elmermetrasbrum@hotmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3e.dts | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3e.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3e.dts
index d3665067c..10e568262 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3e.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3e.dts
@@ -20,4 +20,16 @@ &rgmii_phy1 {

 &gmac1 {
 	status = "okay";
+};
+/*
+ * UART4 on the 40-pin GPIO header (pin 16 = UART4_RX/GPIO3_B1, pin 18 =
+ * UART4_TX/GPIO3_B2 - confirmed against Radxa's own hardware-interface
+ * docs: https://docs.radxa.com/en/zero/zero3/hardware-design/hardware-interface).
+ * Disabled by default (rk356x.dtsi) on the m0 pinmux group, which isn't
+ * wired to any header pin on this board - m1 is the one Radxa actually
+ * routed out. uart4m1_xfer is defined in rk3568-pinctrl.dtsi.
+ */
+&uart4 {
+	status = "okay";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&uart4m1_xfer>;
 };
\ No newline at end of file
